// - Field and enum numbers are never reused. When a field, enum value or
//   oneof arm is removed, its number and name are added to a `reserved`
//   statement in the same message or enum.
// - Numbers 1 to 15 (one-byte tags) go to fields that appear on hot paths.
// - Numbers 1000 to 1999 in any message are reserved for experimental fields.
//   They are only populated when the matching `experimental.*` capability is
//   advertised, and may be removed without a major version bump.
// - Every enum's zero value is `*_UNSPECIFIED` and means "not set". Servers
//   substitute the documented default for it.
// - Unknown enum values must be tolerated by clients (treated as
//   UNSPECIFIED) and by servers (rejected with INVALID_ARGUMENT).
// - A breaking change requires a new package (`cua.env.v2`) served next to
//   v1 until all SDKs have moved.

